==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|slepan|slēpan}}
* {{l|ang|slapan|slāpan}} {{qualifier|Anglian}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|slēpanan|lang=gem-pro}}, from Indo-European ''*leb-, *lob-''.  Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|slepa|slēpa|lang=ofs}}, Old High German ''[[slafan|slāfan]]'' (German ''[[schlafen]]''), Old Saxon {{term|slapan|slāpan|lang=osx}} (Dutch ''[[slapen]]''), Gothic [[𐍃𐌻𐌴𐍀𐌰𐌽]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈslæːp.ɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=strong|class=VII|head=slǣpan}} ({{Latinx|'''slǣpþ'''}} ‘he sleeps’; {{Latinx|'''slēp'''}} ‘he slept’; {{Latinx|'''slēpon'''}} ‘they slept’; {{Latinx|'''ġeslǣpen'''}} past participle)

# to [[sleep]]

